Common InterventionEffectiveness
    documentation "Measurement of the effectiveness of the intervention per diagnosis."
    descriptor Diagnosis
        documentation "Targeted purpose of the intervention (e.g., attendance issue, dropout risk) for which the effectiveness is measured."
        is part of identity
    descriptor PopulationServed
        documentation "Population for which effectiveness is measured."
        is part of identity
    descriptor GradeLevel
        documentation "Grade level for which effectiveness is measured."
        is part of identity
    integer ImprovementIndex
        documentation "Along a percentile distribution of students, the improvement index represents the change in an average student's percentile rank that is considered to be due to the intervention."
        is optional
    descriptor InterventionEffectivenessRating
        documentation "An intervention demonstrates effectiveness if the research has shown that the program caused an improvement in outcomes. Values: positive effects, potentially positive effects, mixed effects, potentially negative effects, negative effects, and no discernible effects."
        is required